{
  "title": "DIP and PIP Joint Arthritis",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/hand/6055/dip-and-pip-joint-arthritis",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Nov 19 2024",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Arthritis of the DIP and PIP joints are very common forms of osteoarthritis seen in the hand and can be associated with pain and deformity.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made radiographically with joint space narrowing seen in the DIP and PIP joints of the fingers. Mucous cysts are often present on clinical inspection of the DIP joint.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is observation if patient is minimally symptomatic. Operative mucous cyst excision, osteophyte resection, or joint fusion may be indicated depending on severity of symptoms and the stage of disease.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Common",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "DIP arthritis is the most common arthritis of the hand",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "DIP > thumb CMC > PIP > MCP",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Forms include",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**primary osteoarthritis**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "DIP",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "highest joint forces in hand",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "undergoes more wear and tear",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "associated with **Heberden's nodules** (caused by osteophytes)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6055/images/dip%20pip%20arthritis..jpg",
                          "caption": "Herberden nodes and Bouchard nodes"
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**mucous cysts**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6055/images/mucous-cyst-with-no-nail-in.jpg",
                          "caption": "mucous cyst"
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "can lead to draining sinus",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "septic arthritis",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "nail ridging",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [
                            {
                              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6055/images/mucous%20cyst_moved.jpg",
                              "caption": ""
                            }
                          ],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "nail can be involved",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "splitting/ridging",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "deformity",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "loss of gloss",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "PIP",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**Bouchard nodes**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6055/images/dip%20pip%20arthritis..jpg",
                          "caption": "Herberden nodes and Bouchard nodes"
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "joint contractures with fibrosis of ligaments",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**erosive osteoarthritis**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "condition is self limiting, patients are relatively asymptomatic, but can be destructive to joint",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "more common in DIP",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "seen in middle aged women with a 10:1 female to male ratio",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms of primary osteoarthritis",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "deformity",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Symptoms of erosive osteoarthritis",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "intermittent inflammatory episodes",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "articular cartilage and adjacent bone destroyed",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "synovial changes similar to RA but not systemic",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "AP, lateral and oblique of hand",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "erosive osteoarthritis will show cartilage destruction, osteophytes, and subchondral erosion (gull wing deformity)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Diagnosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographic",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "diagnosis confirmed by history, physical exam, and radiographs",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "DIP Arthritis",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "nonoperative",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "observation, NSAIDs",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "indications",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "first line of treatment for mild symptoms",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "operative",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "fusion",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "indications",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "debilitating pain and deformity",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "technique",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "fusion with headless screw has highest fusion rate (nonunion in 10%)",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "2nd and 3rd digit fused in extension",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "4th and 5th digit fused in 10-20° flexion",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "risks",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "too large of screw diameter risks fracture, nailbed deformity",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "-1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "too long of a screw length can result in prominent hardware distally, resulting in fingertip hypersensitivity",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "-1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Mucous Cyst",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "nonoperative",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "observation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "indications",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "first line of treatment as 20-60% spontaneously resolve",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "operative",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "mucous cyst excision + osteophyte resection",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "indications",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "impending rupture",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "may need to do local rotational flap for skin coverage",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "outcome",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "osteophytes MUST be debrided or mucous cyst will recur",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "PIP Arthritis",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "nonoperative",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "observations, NSAIDs",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**indications**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "**first line of treatment in mild symptoms**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "operative",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "collateral ligament excision, volar plate release, osteophyte excision",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "indications",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "predominant contracture with minimal joint involvement",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "fusion",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "indications",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "**border digits (index and small PIP)**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "**middle and ring finger OA if there is angulation/rotation deformity, ligamentous instability or poor bone stock**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "technique",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "headless screw fixation has highest fusion rates",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "recreate normal cascade of fingers / PIPJ flexion angles",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "text": "index- 30°, long- 35°, ring- 40°, small- 45°",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "1",
                              "children": []
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "silicone arthroplasty for middle and ring PIPJ",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "radial collateral ligament should be intact to tolerate pinch grip",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "unlike pyrocarbon (unconstrained) implants, linked silicone implants do not depend on soft tissue competence (i.e. collateral ligaments, volar plate) for stability",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "indications",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "central digits (long and ring finger)",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "good bone stock",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "no angulation or deformity",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "outcomes",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "Volar approach has better range of motion and lower revision rate, compared to dorsal approach",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "Consistent improvements in pain but no significant improvement in PIPJ ROM, grip strength or outcome scores",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "-1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Erosive osteoarthritis",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "nonoperative",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "splints, NSAIDs",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "indications",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "tolerable symptoms",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "operative",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "fusion",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "indications",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "intolerable deformity",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "technique",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "position of fusion same as above",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
